This product and its modifications:

  New components (the protocol under proto/ and the web admin under web/)
  are original works, as are the agent v1 server endpoints. Files kept
  from the upstream retain their original Apache-2.0 headers, and those
  MDMesh changed say so: "Modified by the MDMesh contributors" under the
  upstream copyright line, or, where the upstream file had no header, a
  "Derived from Headwind MDM" comment. docs/licenses/upstream-files.tsv in
  the source repository lists every file kept from the upstream; a listed
  file that can't carry a comment (JSON) is changed if it differs from the
  upstream file named there; README.md and this file were rewritten for
  MDMesh.

  The Kotlin device agent under agent-android/ is new, but parts of it are
  ported from the Headwind MDM Android agent under Apache-2.0: app install
  and version handling, crash-loop protection, and some Device Owner policy
  code. Those files carry the upstream copyright and license header and
  state what was changed.

