  bash and readline (GPL-3.0) in mdmesh-supervisor, and the Ubuntu
  packages (GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, LGPL...) and the Eclipse Temurin JDK
  (GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception) in mdmesh-server. The Android
  agent contains desugar_jdk_libs (above).

  What each image contains: every MDMesh release on GitHub
  (https://github.com/MDMesh-app/MDMesh/releases) carries a package list
  for each image and platform (mdmesh-<image>-linux-<arch>.packages.tsv),
  naming every package with its exact version and the source package it
  was built from, and the runtimes (JDK, Tomcat, Node, Caddy).
  docs/licenses/images.md in the source repository explains them.

  Where the source is: the corresponding source of those packages is
  published by the distributions they come from, for the versions the
  list names:
    Alpine Linux packages: the build recipes and patches in
      https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports (the branch of the
      image's Alpine release), with their source archives at
      https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/
    Ubuntu packages: the source packages at
      https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/<source package>/<version>
      (or "apt-get source <source package>=<version>")
    Eclipse Temurin: https://github.com/adoptium/jdk17u, at the tag of
      the JDK version the list names
    desugar_jdk_libs: Google publishes its source at
      https://github.com/google/desugar_jdk_libs; the offer below covers
      the exact version in each APK

  Written offer: for at least three years after we last distribute a
  given image or APK release, we will also give anyone who asks, for a
